    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear engine of the offense. With an elite efficiency score of 83.29, **Henderson** benefits from a high-run-environment park and a favorable matchup against Bibee, who struggles with a high xERA of 4.45. While Bibee features an elite catcher behind the plate, the pitcher's slow delivery provides a unique opportunity for **Henderson** to exploit the basepaths, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. Following closely is **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), who faces Cornelio\u2019s vulnerable 5.59 xERA; this matchup presents the highest ceiling for counting stats today, aided by a significant platoon advantage that elevates his base projection. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects strongly at 74.56, leveraging a massive 17% boost from the favorable SP skill matchup against Hughes.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the final UTIL spot, ultimately awarded to **Coby Mayo** (61.85) over **Tommy White** (52.17). While both players faced strong park factors, **Mayo** secured the edge by occupying the #4 spot in the order, providing greater RBI density compared to **White**, whose baseline projection failed to overcome the platoon disadvantage against Soriano. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a locked-in start (66.54) despite a marginal platoon penalty; the projected 10% park boost for his home venue ensures he remains far above our threshold for benching. We remain thin in the OF and utility ranks due to the ongoing IL absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active core to chase stolen bases and maintain our Roto standing. No major weather risks are flagged today, but we are monitoring the lineup for **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** to ensure they maintain their projected spots in the middle of the order.",
